.TH SESSLINT-BUNDLE 1 "" "SessLint 0.5.0" "SessLint Manual"
.SH NAME
sesslint-bundle \- [read\-only] Generate a privacy\-safe diagnostic support bundle and fixture skeleton.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sesslint bundle [\-o | \-\-output OUTPUT] [\-\-json] [\-\-adapter {auto,canonical,claude\-code\-jsonl,codex\-rollout,openai\-agents}] [\-\-profile PROFILE] [\-\-confidence\-min CONFIDENCE_MIN] [\-\-margin\-min MARGIN_MIN] [\-\-strict\-share] [\-q | \-\-quiet] [\-v | \-\-verbose] PATH
.SH DESCRIPTION
[read\-only] Generate a privacy\-safe diagnostic support bundle and fixture skeleton.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B PATH
Path to session file (.json or .jsonl)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-o OUTPUT, \-\-output OUTPUT
Path to output bundle JSON file
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output bundle as JSON to stdout
.TP
.B \-\-adapter {auto,canonical,claude\-code\-jsonl,codex\-rollout,openai\-agents}
Session format adapter (default: auto) Choices: auto, canonical, claude\-code\-jsonl, codex\-rollout, openai\-agents.
.TP
.B \-\-profile PROFILE
Replay validation profile (default: neutral)
.TP
.B \-\-confidence\-min CONFIDENCE_MIN
Minimum confidence threshold for format auto\-detection
.TP
.B \-\-margin\-min MARGIN_MIN
Minimum margin threshold between top candidates for auto\-detection
.TP
.B \-\-strict\-share
Exit 1 without writing output when the source file contains secret\-shaped material (SL009 share_advisory present)
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Suppress non\-error stderr output
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Print debug diagnostics (settings provenance, elapsed) to stderr
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
a clean session exits 0
(also verification passed / dry-run plan generated)
.TP
.B 1
a session with findings exits 1
(also verification failed / repair refused)
.TP
.B 2
an internal tool error exits 2
(also usage error / invalid flags / I/O failure)
.TP
.B 130
Cancelled — interrupted via Ctrl+C or a cooperative cancellation request;
partial outputs are cleaned up.
.SH SEE ALSO
sesslint(1), sesslint\-check(1), sesslint\-completion(1), sesslint\-diff(1).

.nf
Full documentation: the docs/ tree in the source repository
(docs/SPEC.md, docs/codes/, docs/recipes/, docs/adr/, docs/THREAT_MODEL.md),
or the project site.
.fi

